(Regression test: list data must survive multiple reallocations intact.
 Growing to 10000 elements crosses the doubling boundary many times
 (8 -> 16 -> 32 -> ... -> 16384); the sum verifies every element was
 copied correctly on every realloc.)

a list called items is [].
a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 10000, append i to items, increment i.

a number called total is 0.
a number called j is 1.
While j is less than or equal to items's length,
  a number called item is element j of items,
  the total is the total add item,
  increment j.

Print "length: {items's length}".
Print "sum: {total}".
Print "first: {items's first}".
Print "last: {items's last}".
